        "source": "Balamanorama on 6.1.8",
        "finding": "The anabhyasa restriction prevents a new reduplication when san follows an already intensive stem and when a desiderative stem receives nic and the can aorist. This supports treating an extra reduplicative syllable as a substantive composition error. The commentary also notes that such combinations are absent from ordinary usage."
      },
      {
        "url": "https://sanskritdocuments.org/learning_tools/ashtadhyayi/vyakhya/6/6.1.11.htm",
